WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.062
Wide pivot columns are part of the schema.

00:00:03.062 --> 00:00:06.782
If the categories are stable, that is manageable.

00:00:06.782 --> 00:00:13.202
If new products or diagnoses appear frequently, the SQL must change to add columns.

00:00:13.202 --> 00:00:19.997
Long form handles dynamic categories more naturally because new categories become new rows.

00:00:19.997 --> 00:00:24.872
Often a BI tool can create the presentation matrix from long data.

00:00:24.872 --> 00:00:30.332
Static pivots are easier to read and validate when the category set is known.

00:00:30.332 --> 00:00:33.797
Dynamic pivots are useful when categories change,

00:00:33.797 --> 00:00:38.987
but they introduce schema variability that downstream dashboards or models must handle.

00:00:38.987 --> 00:00:44.240
Discover categories first and decide whether a changing column set is acceptable.
